1. In the frontend (`src/App.tsx`), in a `useEffect`, we fetch the history from the backend:
   ```typescript
   useEffect(() => {
     fetch("/api/history")
       .then(res => res.json())
       .then(data => {
         if (Array.isArray(data) && data.length > 0) {
           setHistory(data);
         } else {
           // If backend has no history, we can upload the frontend seedHistory to the backend to persist it!
           const seeds = seedHistory();
           setHistory(seeds);
           // save to backend
           fetch("/api/history/seed", {
             method: "POST",
             headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
             body: JSON.stringify({ history: seeds })
           }).catch(() => {});
         }
       })
       .catch(() => {
         // fallback to local seed if server fails
         setHistory(seedHistory());
       });
   }, []);
   ```
This is extremely clever! It means the frontend handles the seeding logic, and if the backend has no data, the frontend pushes the seed history to the backend `/api/history/seed` to initialize it!
